    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d869">

                <pb facs="0699" n="583" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12787.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Vice Consul Silliman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-09T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 9, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Brazilian Minister cables requesting Department to transmit to Carranza’s
                    Secretary of War the following:</p>
                <p>[Quotes the message contained in the Minster’s No. 119, August 8.]</p>
                <p>Please bring this to the immediate attention of General Carranza and urge upon
                    him the importance of continuing negotiations in a <pb facs="0700" n="584"
                        xml:id="pg584"/> conciliatory spirit until a basis is reached for the
                    peaceful transfer of authority. We feel confident President Carbajal will agree
                    to any reasonable conditions. Department will gladly transmit Carranza’s
                    reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
